From: pat <pi3iman@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] lib: add test_nftsetbench nft-set-shaped hash call-site A/B module

Gate-4 companion to test_hashbench (docs/umash-port-task.md): A/Bs
jhash against the scalar rapidhash V3 Nano low^high fold through
complete nft-set-shaped lookups - hash + reciprocal_scale/bucket math
+ chain walk + memcmp - on the live kernel, no call-site patches, no
reflash. Two structures faithful to net/netfilter/nft_set_hash.c: a
replication of the fixed nft_hash backend and the real lib/rhashtable
driven like nft_rhash (cmp-arg key, hashfn/obj_hashfn/obj_cmpfn).
Matrix: klen {16,32,48} x population {1024,65536} x pattern {hot-hit,
cold-hit, cold-miss}; every table is verified (all inserted keys
found, absent keys not) before timing.

First run 2026-07-11 on the live router: nano32 won 35/36 cells by
20-80 cy/lookup (hash delta carries through; -15..-30% cache-warm),
compressing to -3..-8% at 64k-population cold misses where cache
stalls dominate. Verdict recorded in the task doc: technically passes
gate 4 but no conversion patch until a real workload profile shows
nft set lookups hot.

Same measurement infra as test_hashbench: dependent-latency chaining,
IRQ-off min-of-chunks, direct A53 PMU register reads, standard exports
only, -EAGAIN on purpose so re-runs need no rmmod.

